Plan: docs/MAINNET_TEST_PLAN.md §6 T3b, stage 1a ("go run ./simhtlc … -paths reclaim, or the same with -regtest …
does steps 1–4 itself"). Machine paths are written <repo>, <tmp>, <user>.

Command (from <repo>/tools; simhtlc built with go1.26.8 at fbe3901; below-normal priority):
  go run ./simhtlc -regtest -prover "wsl.exe -e <path to the pinned proof-xmr build>" -paths reclaim -state-dir <tmp>/st/t3b-regtest
The plan's -regtest form, with -state-dir for §4. It took 2,032 s (about 34 minutes; the plan says about 35).

What simhtlc did (steps 1–4, from its raw output below)
  1. bob locked and paid the stipend, then was stopped once in watching_xmr;
  2. alice locked her XMR (866a87d0…) and was stopped at height 2955 in await_refund, before t2 2979;
  3. bob came back at height 2968, his refund cutoff (t2 − 11): "height 2968 is at or past the refund cutoff 2968 (t2
     2979 − 11) with the lock open: no Refund is sent", then refund_window -> punish_window; nobody punished in
     [2979, 3009); at t2 + g2 he Reclaimed ("reclaimed the lock nobody punished: tx 07157fe4… at height 3009"),
     reclaiming -> reclaim_confirming, and ended reclaimed once it was stable (stable height 3011);
  4. alice was restarted from her state file at height 3009 (t2 + g2), sent no Punish, read s_b ("bob reclaimed the
     lock after t2 + g2; s_b read from the chain"), await_refund -> refund_seen -> sweep_ready -> sweeping -> swept.
  The plan's step 4 says she "moves to await_reclaim". Restarted at t2 + g2 itself, she did not pass through
  await_reclaim: the Reclaim was already in the pool, and she went from await_refund to refund_seen once st_0 was 4.
  Her companion enters await_reclaim only while the lock is still open past her Punish cutoff (tools/xmrswap/swap.go,
  around line 2421); T3c exercises it.

